	1.	Prepare the presentation – Create slides explaining the project, objectives, features, and technologies used.
	2.	Introduce the project – Explain the problem and the proposed solution.
	3.	Explain the system – Describe the main modules and how they work.
	4.	Demonstrate the project – Show the actual working system step by step.
	5.	Show important features – Demonstrate the major functions of the project.
	6.	Explain the results – Present the output and benefits of the system.
	7.	Answer questions – Respond to questions from teachers or evaluators.
	8.	Collect feedback – Note suggestions for improvements.
